<title>Lesson Activities</title>
<para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.11.1: Changing the Graphing Window </item>
  <item> 5.11.2: Choosing an Appropriate Model </item>
  <list>
    <item> 5.11.2: Self Check  </item>
    <item> 5.11.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.11.3: Modeling with Exponential Functions </item>
  <item> 5.11.4: Examine Exponential Decay in Context </item>
  <list>
    <item> 5.11.4: Self Check  </item>
    <item> 5.11.4: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.11.5: Using Relationship Models to Answer Questions </item>
</list>
<para>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 5.11.6: Practice.</para>
<title>Required Materials</title>
<list>
  <item> A collection of balls that bounce (extension activity) </item>
  <item> Measuring tapes (extension activity) </item>
  <item> Graphing technology </item>
</list>
<title>Required Preparation</title>
<para>Graphing technology should be available if students request it. Measuring tapes and balls that bounce are only needed
  if doing the extension activity.</para>
<title>Lesson Vocabulary</title>
<para>During this lesson, it is important to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Familiarize students with the vocabulary words they will see throughout the lesson. Encourage students to look
    for these words and notice their use and meanings. </item>
  <item> Encourage students to use key vocabulary words in “math talk” and their written and oral
    explanations. </item>
  <item> Utilize a word wall. Sample cards are located here: <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/8ed3aa68763498713b44d3c2e537ffe61b4755f0">Mathematics Vocabulary Word Wall Cards</link> </item>
</list>
<para>Vocabulary words that are emphasized in this lesson include:</para>
